define host_git_schema returning Str:
    return "{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"host_git\",\"description\":\"Admin Git workflow at an absolute repository/directory path using installed Git. Supply one subcommand as operation and separate argument strings: status, diff, log, show, grep, ls-files, branch/switch, add/commit, apply, merge/rebase, worktree, remote/fetch/push, clone or other native Git commands. For init/clone, repository is the existing working directory. Output and raw exit status are durably captured; inspect with workspace_output_next. No shell concatenation or pager. Writes/network are governed by the initiating admin audience and host protected-root/secret policy; protected Echo changes still require the charter controller. Commands can alter history or remote state: use only for the authorized task, inspect status/diff first, preserve unrelated changes and inspect retained results before retrying uncertain operations. Never put tokens/passwords in arguments. Exit code 1 can mean differences/no matches for some Git commands; interpret their output.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"repository\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"operation\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"arguments\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"}}},\"required\":[\"repository\",\"operation\",\"arguments\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}}"
